course: dictionary
lesson: 8148
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. Republican is a good example. A small r, as in «a republican», usually means a person who wants their country to be a republic, ruled by elected leaders with no king or queen.
explain: A capital R, as in «the Republicans», often means a member of the Republican Party, one of the two big parties in the USA. The clues are the words around it. In «the Republicans (an elephant)», the elephant and the parties tell you it is about US politics.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning. If it does not, try another meaning.
fact: A republic is a country with elected leaders and no king or queen.
fact: «Republican» with a small r means a person who wants their country to be a republic.
fact: «Republican» with a capital R often means a member of the Republican Party in the USA.
fact: The Republicans' symbol is an elephant and their colour is red, so TV maps often show them in red.
fact: In Ireland, a republican is a person who wants a united, independent Ireland.
exercise: «That is why the map on election night turns states red or blue: red usually means the Republicans.» Which colour usually means the Republicans? | Green | Yellow | *Red | Blue
exercise: «The Democrats (whose cartoon symbol is a donkey) and the Republicans (an elephant).» What is the cartoon symbol of the Democrats? | A bear | An elephant | *A donkey | A lion
exercise: A republican wants their country to be a republic. What does a republican want? | To stop all elections | To join another country | A king or queen to rule forever | *Elected leaders, with no king or queen
test: Mia says only Americans can be republicans. Is she right? | Yes, only Americans can be republicans | *No, anyone can want their country to be a republic | No, because republicans have kings | Yes, because republicans always wear red
test: In «the Republicans (an elephant)», which meaning fits best? | A person who wants a republic, with no king | A small country near Ireland | A map of the election results | *A member of the Republican Party in the USA
exam: What is the best way to work out which meaning of republican is used? | Ask a friend and never check | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Guess the first meaning you see | Skip the word forever
